    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full build passes. \n\nThe change is complete. Summary of the soft-delete implementation, kept to small, low-complexity edits:\n\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `boolean deleted` field (defaults `false`) with compact one-line `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()` accessors.\n- **`function/owner/DeleteOwner.java`** \u2014 `DELETE /api/owners/{id}` now flags `owner.setDeleted(true)` and `save`s (retaining the row, returning 204) instead of removing it.\n- **`function/owner/EnsureUniqueIdentity.java`** & **`EnsureUniqueHousehold.java`** \u2014 the create endpoint's duplicate/identity loops now skip owners where `isDeleted()`, so a match against a deleted owner no longer blocks creation (one extra `&&` condition each).\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` (via MapStruct, mapped by name) serializes it; `GET` now returns `deleted`.\n- **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** + **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 added the `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` column (the hsqldb test profile uses `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema and the positional seed inserts needed the column).\n\nBehavior verified: a new owner reads back `deleted:false`; after `DELETE` the record is retained and reads back `deleted:true`; and a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed once the only matching owner is soft-deleted. Full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nI did not touch the mysql/postgres schemas \u2014 those DB profiles aren't exercised by the tests, and the app's default `h2` profile auto-adds the column via `ddl-auto=update`. Let me know if you'd like those production schemas updated too for consistency.",
